"VMMaker.oscog-cb.3826: enforce a minimum new space size so that each survivor space is at least 200Kb.  Since VMMaker.oscog-cb.3825 the Cogit compiles abstract instructions and fixups in the future survivor space, so a small eden (e.g. -eden 1m on the command line, or vmParameterAt: 45 put: in the image header) made the survivor spaces too small to compile large methods, which then fell back to the interpreter (MethodTooBig).  SpurMemoryManager>>edenBytes: now enforces minEdenBytes, i.e. scavengerDenominator * 200Kb.  The simulator's facade, which wants an empty new space, assigns edenBytes directly."!!SpurMemoryManager methodsFor: 'scavenger' stamp: 'cb 10/27/2026 14:00'!minEdenBytes	"Answer the minimum size of new space, excluding the interpreter allocation reserve.  Each survivor	 space is a scavengerDenominator'th of it.  The Cogit compiles abstract instructions and fixups in the	 future survivor space (see Cogit>>allocateOpcodes:bytecodes:ifFail:), so keep the survivor spaces	 at least 200Kb to be able to compile large methods."	^self scavengerDenominator * 200 * 1024! !!SpurMemoryManager methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/27/2026 14:00'!edenBytes: bytes	"Set the size of new space, excluding the interpreter allocation reserve.  The desired size can be	 set arbitrarily small (command line, vmParameterAt: 45 put:), so enforce minEdenBytes."	edenBytes := bytes max: self minEdenBytes! !!Spur32BitCoMemoryManager methodsFor: 'debug support' stamp: 'cb 10/27/2026 14:00'!setUpForUseByFacade: aCurrentImageCoInterpreterFacade	"Make sure that eden etc are initialized, so that methods can be printed.	 This is really to make addressCouldBeObj: et al work.	 Assign edenBytes directly; edenBytes: would enforce minEdenBytes."	<doNotGenerate>	edenBytes := 0.	self setHeapBase: self freeStart		memoryLimit: self endOfMemory		endOfMemory: self endOfMemory! !!Spur64BitCoMemoryManager methodsFor: 'debug support' stamp: 'cb 10/27/2026 14:00'!setUpForUseByFacade: aCurrentImageCoInterpreterFacade	"Make sure that eden etc are initialized, so that methods can be printed.	 This is really to make addressCouldBeObj: et al work.	 Assign edenBytes directly; edenBytes: would enforce minEdenBytes."	<doNotGenerate>	edenBytes := 0.	self setHeapBase: self freeStart		memoryLimit: self endOfMemory		endOfMemory: self endOfMemory! !